# madcide keybinding profile: Thonny's keys (plan §41.11a step 3e) — each
# command's `default_sequence` in Thonny's source (github.com/thonny/thonny,
# master, read 2026-09-30) onto the one action vocabulary. `primary` is
# Ctrl, or Cmd on macOS: Thonny binds each command both ways. Thonny's
# editor is Tk's text widget: Ctrl+arrows move by word, Ctrl+Home and
# Ctrl+End go to the ends, and Shift with any motion selects (the engine's
# rule, so it needs no lines here). Those motions keep their Ctrl keys on
# macOS too (Tk's Option-arrow word motion there is not bound: a profile
# has one key per binding).
#
# Thonny's keys whose command madcide does not have yet are listed, not
# invented: File ▸ New (Ctrl+N), Close (Ctrl+W), Close all (Ctrl+Shift+W);
# Edit ▸ Auto-complete (Ctrl+Space); Run ▸ Interrupt (Ctrl+C in the Shell —
# here Ctrl+C copies everywhere and Ctrl+F2 stops), Send EOF (Ctrl+D), the
# debugger (F6, F7, F8, Ctrl+F5, Shift+F5, Ctrl+F8); View ▸ the font size
# (Ctrl+plus, Ctrl+minus) and Full screen (F11). Thonny's Find & Replace is one dialog on Ctrl+F: here
# Ctrl+F finds, and Edit ▸ Replace… is the menu's row (no key of its own).
@title Thonny

# File
primary+o editfile
primary+s save
primary+shift+s saveas
primary+alt+s saveall
primary+q quit
alt+f4 quit
# Edit
primary+z undo
primary+y redo
primary+x cut
primary+c copy
primary+v paste
primary+a selectall
# Indent / Dedent selected lines are Thonny's Tab and Shift+Tab: Tab over
# a selection that crosses a line indents it (the editor's GUI rule, no
# line here); Shift+Tab dedents the selection's lines, or the caret's.
shift+tab dedent
primary+3 togglecomment
primary+f find
primary+g gotoline
primary+l replclear
# Run: F5 runs the script into the Shell's session (a fresh one, its
# names left for the prompt); Ctrl+F2 is Stop/Restart backend.
f5 replrun
primary+f2 replstop
# Tk's text motions
ctrl+left wordleft
ctrl+right wordright
ctrl+home top
ctrl+end bottom
# The project window's keys (@project scope — profile data; the baked
# defaults add esc/backspace).
@project ins projadd
@project del projdel
@project enter projopen
